cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mapgis2shp: open-source interoperability and original-library rendering for legacy MapGIS 6.x/67 vector data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
abstract: >-
  mapgis2shp (import name pymapgis) is an open-source Python reader and
  writer for the MapGIS 6.x/67 closed binary vector formats (.wt point, .wl
  line, .wp polygon). It reverse-engineers the on-disk layout, infers the
  coordinate reference system, reconstructs and regenerates polygon topology,
  decodes graphic parameters and structural graphic libraries, renders vectors
  from the original graphic libraries, and exchanges data with GeoPandas
  GeoDataFrames / shapefiles, enabling Chinese
  geological-survey data locked in the proprietary MapGIS format to enter
  the open-source geospatial stack and return to it.
version: "2.7.1"
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/leecugb/mapgis2shp
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24036158
keywords:
  - MapGIS
  - GIS
  - vector
  - geopandas
  - shapefile
  - reverse-engineering
  - geology
